@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE REP PITCH CARD, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        <div class="view-object-backdrop rep-backdrop">
            @* #997 · AND HE GETS A WAY OUT THAT IS NOT AN ANSWER. #992's register has this card down as a
               critical-DECISION modal — allowed no ✕ only because every answer it offers is itself a close
               — and that row was never driven, so nothing ever pressed it. Read AnswerTheRep: THREE of his
               six moves leave the card up. Buying refreshes the pitch to the tier you now hold, "I already
               have a policy" sets his reply beside it, and "that is not my name" re-pitches under the
               corrected name. Only "not today" and "good day" send him to the bar. So the claim was false,
               and the honest fix is the one the ruling asks for first: a way out that is not a decision.

               A BARE frame, because .view-object is a flex column whose foot is pinned by
               `.view-object > .view-object-close` — the dismiss has to be a DIRECT child of the card, and
               a shell that wrapped it would quietly unstick twenty other cards' buttons too. *@
            <OverlayShell class="view-object rep-card" StopClicks="true"
                          Frame="OverlayFrame.Bare" Dismiss="OverlayDismiss.Close"
                          DismissClass="view-object-close" DismissFace="Step away"
                          DismissLabel="Step away from the rep"
                          DismissTitle="Leave the pitch where it is — he keeps the file, and the bar keeps him"
                          OnClose="() => Dismiss(CloseTheRepsCard)">
                <div class="view-object-title">@SpaceSails.Core.NebulaRep.DisplayName</div>
                <img class="view-object-img rep-portrait" src="@SpaceSails.Core.NebulaRep.PortraitArt"
                     alt="@SpaceSails.Core.NebulaRep.RepName" onerror="this.style.display='none'" />
                <div class="rep-desk">@SpaceSails.Core.NebulaRep.Desk</div>
                <div class="view-object-caption rep-pitch">@pitch.Line</div>
                @if (_repSaid is { Length: > 0 } saidBack)
                {
                    <div class="rep-said">@saidBack</div>
                }
                <div class="rep-offers">
                    @foreach (var repOffer in pitch.Offers)
                    {
                        var repMove = repOffer.Move;
                        <button type="button" class="rep-offer" @onclick="() => Dismiss(() => AnswerTheRep(repMove))">@repOffer.Label</button>
                    }
                </div>
            </OverlayShell>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    /// <summary>the page's `string? _repSaid`</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? _repSaid { get; set; }
    /// <summary>the page's `void AnswerTheRep(NebulaRep.RepMove move)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action<NebulaRep.RepMove> AnswerTheRep { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `void CloseTheRepsCard()`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action CloseTheRepsCard { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `Task Dismiss(Action close)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>bound by the @if that stays in the page</summary>
    [Parameter] public NebulaRep.RepPitch pitch { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
